    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d600">

                <pb facs="0827" n="703" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg703"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.74/118</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">of a Conversation
                        with the Ecuadoran Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Elizalde</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I sent for the Minister of Ecuador and referred to his inquiry of a week ago in
                    regard to the opening of negotiations by his Government with Panama, with a view
                    to the control of wireless messages between the two countries. I explained to
                    the Minister that in view of the terms of the Treaty of 1903 with Panama, and of
                    Decree #130, issued by the Government of Panama, August 29, 1914, we had certain
                    vested rights in the control of wireless in Panama.</p>
                <p>I suggested that it might be preferable to delay negotiations until the
                    forthcoming Inter-American Communications Conference, when the whole subject of
                    electrical communications for this hemisphere would be discussed. I thought that
                    after the conclusion of the Conference, <pb facs="0828" n="704" xml:id="pg704"/>
                    if his Government desired to take up such negotiations, that they might again
                    approach the subject through the Department.</p>
                <p>The Minister replied that he had reached the same conclusion and it would be
                    preferable, before taking any action in the matter, to await the results of the
                    Inter-American Communications Conference.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d600-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed>W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">illiam</hi>] P[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">hillips</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
